# Claude geez archive

> A Claude conversation archive on the geez thread (the MCP tool that lets a client call Grok).

## Purpose
Explain this repo as saved talk about geez, not as the tool itself. Source: fitzyracing1/claude-geez.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the chat history in this repo.
2. Use it to recall how geez was designed.
3. Run the real tool from fitzyracing1/geez.

## Key ideas
- Conversation archive
- geez thread
- Family of claude-* repos

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/claude-geez
archive = conversation_shelf("geez")
read(archive)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. conversation_shelf("geez") → “this folder holds that thread”
2. read(archive) → “open the saved talk”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader wants the running MCP tool → send them to geez
- If a reader wants the chat → stay here

## What a person would notice
Talk about the pipe, not the pipe itself.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the archive, or geez.
